    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 7 with a high-upside offensive core, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), who registers as our top play today against Lowder. While his batting order slot is suboptimal, the combination of a favorable 4.77 xERA matchup, a significant platoon advantage, and wind assistance creates an elite environment for his speed-oriented profile. Joining him in the \"Strong\" start tier are **Junior Caminero** (69.27) and **Trea Turner** (68.63). **Junior Caminero** benefits from a soft matchup against Bennett, and while he is currently in a \"Lineup Pending\" status, his projected #3 spot ensures high-leverage opportunities. **Trea Turner** remains a cornerstone of our stolen base strategy, as the slow delivery of Ginn provides a tangible boost to his already high-ceiling projection.\n\nThe decision to slot **Kyle Schwarber** (62.66) into the UTIL position was bolstered by his strong .392 xwOBA, helping him edge out marginal internal candidates for the start. Conversely, **Caleb Durbin** (41.71) serves as our most volatile inclusion; his score is dragged down significantly by a #9 spot in the order and a challenging matchup against Griffin Jax (3.02 xERA). However, **Caleb Durbin** remains in the lineup purely for his elite SB potential, as we are prioritizing speed-first assets even against tough pitching. With **Yordan Alvarez**, **Christian Yelich**, **Hyeseong Kim**, and **Kazuma Okamoto** all unavailable due to scheduling or injury, the bench remains thin, leaving little room for error if we hope to maintain our pace in the 5x5 standings. We are also monitoring the availability of **Colt Keith**, **Carson Benge**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Zac Veen**, **Luke Raley**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** should late-scratch scenarios arise.",
